diff --git a/NativeARM/host/XRIZER.md b/NativeARM/host/XRIZER.md
index ff1a296..b387645 100644
--- a/NativeARM/host/XRIZER.md
+++ b/NativeARM/host/XRIZER.md
@@ -1,5 +1,10 @@
 # Native xrizer host adapter
 
+Current checkpoint: private-memory ABI translation is user-authorized. The
+constrained host now runs only with explicit `--run-constrained`. Actual Valve
+Lua allocator tests and a headless Source2Main/xrizer startup pass as described
+at the end. Earlier preflight-only restrictions below record prior milestones.
+
 Build without VeRantyx's renderer/readback objects:
 
 ```sh
@@ -118,3 +123,83 @@ The constrained host's unconditional execution gate remains in place.
 Klepton's separate `KL_VK_STRICT=1` mode now preserves graphics requests and
 returns driver errors rather than using its legacy feature repair/stub paths;
 see `VULKAN_BACKENDS.md` in that checkout for native driver tests.
+
+
+## Authorized ABI translation and first headless startup
+
+The user authorized necessary private-memory ABI translation on 20 October.
+Installed game binaries remain unchanged; kl_luafix/kl_guestfix are excluded.
+`HOST_MODE=constrained` remains default-blocked until `--run-constrained` is
+explicitly passed. It then forces strict Vulkan, managed thread tracking,
+trap-code SVC handling and generic patch-table off. It forces real constructors
+on and clears constructor-skip/pretranslated-image overrides. A pre-constructor
+hook rejects unresolved imports, ABI refusals and untrapped SVC candidates.
+It installs the Lua setter replacement for both probes and engine execution.
+
+`valve-lua-test` now exercises the actual owner's libvscript with GNU C++/unwind
+runtime dependencies from verified Debian package-index hashes. Three rounds
+check strings up to 8 MiB, 262144-element table growth and contents, full GC,
+zero live Lua mappings after close, and allocation failure/recovery. Three
+mremap attempts return ENOSYS and successfully fall back. The real ELF setter
+GOT binding is checked; the original low-address Lua branch remains unchanged.
+No Lua/video text patch is installed. Actual engine Lua setup/VR play remains
+unverified. The C `floor` function is now correctly forwarded, rather than
+left unresolved.
+
+`valve-preflight` enables KL_LOAD_NO_INIT for mapping/relocation only. Engine,
+Vulkan renderer, VR, video and client modules pass with zero unresolved imports
+and translation refusals. libvideo has 1703 SVC sites, all converted to reserved
+fatal BRK markers; they are NOT assumed harmless or replaced with NOPs. Any
+executed marker stops with an unsupported-operation diagnostic. These are not
+working Linux raw syscall semantics. All five constructor probes subsequently
+pass, including the client, without reaching a marker or glibc zero stub.
+
+The new scripts are explicit, isolated tools:
+
+- fetch_lua_runtime.py fetches selected Debian ARM64 runtime packages over HTTPS,
+  verifies package sizes/SHA256 against the recorded index, extracts libraries
+  and copyright files, and installs nothing. Default packages are libstdc++6
+  and libgcc-s1; libuuid1 is also supported for engine tests.
+- clone_game_root.py creates a NEW APFS clonefile content root, overlays original
+  ARM64 depot files, and refuses existing outputs/full-copy fallback/input
+  symlinks. Cloned files have separate inodes; writing a clone is tested to
+  preserve source bytes. It does not use the old rm-rf/symlink content script.
+- prepare_guest_dir.py creates a NEW flat ELF library lookup directory. Exact
+  filenames take priority over generated SONAME aliases, retaining distinct
+  .so/.so.N inputs. Adreno ICD/mimalloc exclusions match the existing host path.
+- run_valve_lua.py creates a NEW isolated test directory, derives setter/branch
+  locations from the actual ELF, bounds execution and hashes all five libraries
+  before/after. It never invokes Source2Main.
+- launch_xrizer.py uses xrizer's dual-ICD wrapper/census, requires a cloned root,
+  isolates OpenVR registry, guest HOME, cache/config and Steam-discovery files,
+  and records command/environment/results. Native Darwin HOME stays unchanged.
+  The Steam bridge uses the real running macOS client and ownership/authentication
+  path; constrained launches refuse a missing client instead of fabricating a
+  process ID. They do not write the real ~/.steam discovery files.
+
+A bounded `--no-xr-runtime` startup reached Source2Main, loaded the real macOS
+Steam client and native xrizer, then hit the deliberate OpenXR-unavailable
+checkpoint. The process exited 0 on the engine's VR failure path; that is NOT
+successful gameplay. The explicit invalid XR_RUNTIME_JSON prevents runtime
+fallback, so Monado/headset access was excluded. Steam client loading and API
+callbacks were observed; full gameplay/ownership progression was not proven by
+this early-exit run.
+
+For the first user headset test, from this checkout:
+
+```sh
+python3 NativeARM/scripts/launch_xrizer.py \
+  --root /private/tmp/alyx-native-game-root \
+  --libs /private/tmp/alyx-native-guest-libs-ready \
+  --output /private/tmp/alyx-monado-first \
+  --runtime-json /Users/nickkennedy/Code/monado-2/build/arm64/openxr_monado-dev.json \
+  --timeout 120
+```
+
+Native macOS Steam must be running and signed in to the owning account. This
+uses MoltenVK by default. Output must be new for each run. Logs are under
+`backend/run.log`, with driver census and launch manifests beside it. The first
+test should establish whether it reaches the menu and draws stereo correctly;
+no headset/GPU-frame benchmark or actual foveation API trace is claimed yet.
+KosmicKrisp selection is available with --driver kosmickrisp --icd PATH, but its
+known missing VK_EXT_metal_objects still blocks Monado interoperability.
